course: dictionary
lesson: 2368
title: Finding the culprit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A culprit is the person who has done something wrong, or the thing that causes a problem. When you meet a new word, look at the clues around it.
explain: «His dad went detective and found the culprit in the next room: Leo's sister, streaming a film in high quality.» The clues are detective and found. A detective looks for the person who did wrong, so culprit must mean the guilty person. Try the swap: «Who did it?» fits, so your meaning works.
explain: Culprit can also mean the cause of a problem, not a person. In science, «sugar is the culprit for tooth decay» means sugar is what causes the teeth to rot. Ask yourself: is this about a person who did wrong, or about what made something go wrong?
fact: A culprit is the person who has done something wrong or committed a crime.
fact: A culprit can also be the cause of a problem, such as sugar causing tooth decay.
fact: «The main culprit» means the biggest cause of a problem.
fact: «The guilty culprit» means the person who did the wrong thing.
fact: Culprit is a noun. You can have one culprit or several culprits.
exercise: «His dad went detective and found the culprit in the next room.» Who was the culprit? | Leo's dad, who was the detective | The next room itself | The internet, which was robbed | *Leo's sister, who was streaming a film
exercise: «Sugar is the culprit for tooth decay.» What is the culprit in this sentence? | A happy, healthy smile | A dentist who fixes teeth | The toothbrush that cleans the teeth | *The cause of the trouble, here sugar
exercise: Mum says, «Who broke the window? Find the culprit!» What is a culprit? | The window that got broken | The detective who asks the questions | A tool for fixing windows | *The person who did the wrong thing
test: Dad says, «The real culprit is the cold, not the football.» What does the real culprit mean? | A cold drink on a hot day | The person who plays football | *The true cause of the problem | The football that was kicked
test: Which word means the person who has done something wrong? | *culprit | curtain | cupboard | cushion
exam: «The guilty culprit left a muddy footprint by the back door.» What does culprit mean here? | A muddy path in the garden | *The person who did the wrong thing | A footprint in the mud | A back door that was left open
